      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i was reading about box breathing (like the 4-4-4-4 thing) and was wondering what it actually does to the body? like how does that specific rhythm affect my nervous system or cortisol?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing, the 4-4-4-4 rhythm, is a simple yet powerful tool for calming the nervous system. It works by deliberately slowing down your breathing rate, which sends a signal to your brain that you are safe, effectively shifting you out of the \"fight or flight\" mode. This shift helps to lower your heart rate and can significantly reduce levels of stress hormones like cortisol. By controlling your breath, you are essentially giving your body a moment of quiet, which is very restorative.",
      "source": "target",
